WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.033
-You know, this is --

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.133
this is your 14th appearance
on our show,

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:05.467
and I'm so grateful.
-It is?

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:06.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Isn't that wild?

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:08.033
-Wow.
-I --

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.000
-Thank you.
I have to thank you

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.033
because when
you're first getting started,

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:14.100
it's not easy
to book these shows,

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.033
and you've been in my corner
since the very beginning,

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.267
so I thank you.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.501
-We've been through a lot.
-We have been

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:20.133
through a lot together.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.334
-Last time I saw you,

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.601
we did an episode of
"That's My Jam" in L.A.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:25.267
-Yes.
-And you were fantastic.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:27.167
-Thank you.
-Blew the audience away.

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:29.067
-You always give me
great songs, though.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:30.834
-Yeah. Well,
we got to make it good.

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:33.734
I'm sorry about the water.
-[ Sighs ]

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:35.801
-Well, you know,
here's the thing.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:38.267
You knew that was
going to happen, right?

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:40.968
-I'm never prepared for it.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.934
You can't wet Black women's
hair like that.

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:44.501
I told you that, Jimmy.

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:47.400
We turn into Chia Pets right
in front of your very eyes.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.167
You have to give us a heads-up.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:51.767
-You were so -- like, 'cause
we give you protective glasses.

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:53.968
Like...
-I need a shower cap.

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:56.167
[ Laughter ]
An umbrella.

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:57.667
-Next time --
Next time we can do that.

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.367
-Yes.
-You know, I follow you

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:00.968
on the on the socials,

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:03.968
and I saw this amazing
photo of you here.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.534
Explain what was happening here.
[ Audience cheering ]

00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:08.701
-I mean --
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.467
-You may have heard of Beyoncé.
I don't know.

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:13.467
-Yeah, absolutely.
-Well, the thing about it is,

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.501
I had already had
my outfit picked out

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:19.100
for her show months in advance,
and then she does this,

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.100
"Oh, it's my birthday.
Let's all wear silver."

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:26.534
So, I mean, my house
is being renovated,

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:28.367
all of my clothes
are in storage,

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:31.767
and I randomly happened
to just buy this

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:34.000
off of those
Instagram shopping pages.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.200
And when it came,
I was about to throw it away

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.000
because it was like paper thin.
You could see through it.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.467
But at the end of the day,
that's all I had for Beyoncé.

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:45.167
It was kind of silver,
had silver sparklies on it.

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:47.400
Long story short, I had to throw
it away at the end of the night

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.367
because it had snags
and holes and...

00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:50.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.534 --> 00:01:52.334
But thanks, Instagram Shopping!

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:56.400
-I mean,
who else can pull this off?

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.968
-I pulled it off.

00:01:57.968 --> 00:02:00.234
-I can't even imagine
seeing the concert with you

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:02.734
because I think that
you would end up on stage.

00:02:02.734 --> 00:02:04.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.834
And I'll tell you why.
-Why?

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:09.534
-Because I have a photo of you
on stage with Usher.

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:11.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.801
[ Cheering ]

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:14.334
How do you end up --
Of course this is you.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.868
How do you end up
on stage with Usher?

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.601
-Okay, well, it was
my birthday, and my girls

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:20.667
and I decided
to celebrate in Vegas.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:22.234
And we were going
to the Usher concert,

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:24.334
and I kind of knew
something was going to happen

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:25.667
because they were like,
"Sit in this seat!"

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:27.667
I know what
the camera seats are.

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:31.100
So I sat in the seat.
I was so excited.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:35.100
And he came to the stage, and he
wasn't ready to call me up yet.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.901
And he looked over my way
and he was like,

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:39.434
"I see you, Taraji,"
and I thought that was my cue,

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:41.968
so I ran up on the stage
before --

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:43.234
[ Laughter ]
-He's like --

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:45.200
-And he didn't say anything.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.767
-"I see --
Oh, she's coming up!"

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:48.567
-Usher is a female magnet.

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:52.334
I don't know if you know this,
but you're like drawn to him.

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.334
So cut to
I'm in Paris, Fashion Week,

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:56.234
and he's performing there.

00:02:56.234 --> 00:02:57.868
And he's in the audience
doing his thing again,

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:00.534
and he sees Pharrell.
And you know I know Pharrell.

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:03.801
And so he says, "Hey,"
he gives Pharrell his flowers.

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:04.968
Then he looks across,
and he goes,

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:06.434
"Is that Taraji P. Henson?"

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:09.367
And I swear to God,
I took off running.

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:11.601
And there's something about him.
He's a magnet.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:15.033
But you come in twerking.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:17.100
Promise you!
Look at all the footage.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.133
It's not just me!

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:20.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.200
-The way you walk up to Usher,
you just --

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.868
-You just come in twerking.
-You just end up twerking.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:26.100
-That's how it happens.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.767
He's a magnet,
and he pulls it out of you.

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:29.634
I don't twerk.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:31.834
-In public.
-Yeah, in public.

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:33.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:35.300
I want to talk to you
about a couple things,

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.634
because during the pandemic,

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:38.501
you were nice enough
to me and the show.

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:41.868
You Zoomed in when we couldn't
leave the house or get guests.

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:43.634
And you were showing me this.

00:03:43.634 --> 00:03:45.801
You're like, "I'm starting this
new line out of my kitchen."

00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:47.234
-Oh, yes.
-Let's talk about this.

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:49.868
This is TPH.
-Yes.

00:03:49.868 --> 00:03:51.300
-Okay.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.934
Taraji P. Henson,
beauty products, hair...

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:55.834
-Hair and skin.
-And skin.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.234
-Yeah.
-And by the way,

00:03:57.234 --> 00:03:58.501
it's taken off now.

00:03:58.501 --> 00:04:02.200
"Allure" magazine, you got
the Best of Beauty award.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.267
It was three years ago?
-Yeah.

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:07.567
-That's a lot of hard work

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:08.934
-We launched
during the pandemic.

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:11.801
But I think, you know,
my brand, I --

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:15.334
Guys, I also launched
a mental-health foundation

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:16.501
named after my father,

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:17.734
Boris Lawrence Henson
Foundation,

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:19.067
because in the Black
and Brown community,

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:20.868
we really don't talk about it,
and we're dying.

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:22.501
And so it's to eradicate
the stigma

00:04:22.501 --> 00:04:25.200
around mental wellness
in the community.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.133
But also during the pandemic,
everybody was going through it.

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:31.300
We were all feeling
some kind of way depressed

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.634
and not feeling
like ourselves,

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:34.834
and people were afraid
to be out amongst each other.

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:39.133
And so I wanted
to create a spa-like feeling

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:40.901
with products
that you can afford.

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:43.000
-There's a lot of work.
That's three years and now --

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.567
-We're everywhere --
Walmart, CVS, Target.

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:47.567
-I'm so happy for you.
-Yeah. Sally.

00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:50.300
-It couldn't happen
to a better person.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.400
-Thank you.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.534
-And it's a good cause
behind it, too.

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:54.634
Let's talk about "Jaja."
-Oh, guys...

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.267
-This is a big deal.
Just opened tonight.

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:57.868
I'm honored that you're here
with us tonight.

00:04:57.868 --> 00:05:00.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.234
-My first time on Broadway
as a producer.

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:05.701
-"Jaja's African Hair Braiding."
-It's amazing.

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.167
-Can you explain
what it's about?

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:09.667
-So, for me,
what I love about this

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:11.300
is that I grew up
in Washington, D.C.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:14.601
We didn't have a lot of African
braiding salons, right?

00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:17.534
So I was always over at Pookie
or Peaches or somebody's cousin

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:19.868
sitting in between their legs
getting my hair braided.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.501
So this was
an eye-opener for me.

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:23.601
But what struck me
as most interesting

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:26.968
is these women who are literally
like hidden figures,

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:30.133
and they work
in these braiding salons

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.467
in fear of being
deported every day.

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:35.167
And I never --
When you think about deportation

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:39.033
or ICE, all we see
are the Latin faces.

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:41.067
We never see other communities

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:43.234
that are affected
by deportation.

00:05:43.234 --> 00:05:47.534
So that brought -- made me aware
of these humans in another way.

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:51.601
I will never go to Harlem and
bypass one of these

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:53.634
African hair-braiding places
without at least

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:56.968
sticking my head in,
saying hi or something,

00:05:56.968 --> 00:05:59.334
because these are real people
with real lives.

00:05:59.334 --> 00:06:03.434
And this -- this is a really
big piece of our culture.

00:06:03.434 --> 00:06:05.000
I remember working
at the Pentagon.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.434
I would show up one day
with my hair short,

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:09.234
and the next day, I come in
with braids like this,

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:11.534
and they'd be like,
"Yesterday..."

00:06:11.534 --> 00:06:12.834
and I'd be like,
"I ate my spinach."

00:06:12.834 --> 00:06:14.601
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.601 --> 00:06:16.067
But this is a great play.

00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:18.367
If you want to know how Black
hair works, come see the play.

00:06:18.367 --> 00:06:19.868
-There you go, yeah.

00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:22.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:24.467
I will.
-Yeah, but it's a play

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:27.968
by women, for women.
You know, we rock, women, so...

00:06:27.968 --> 00:06:29.701
-You do.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:31.901
And I will say,
Manhattan Theatre Club

00:06:31.901 --> 00:06:33.167
just announced
that the show is getting

00:06:33.167 --> 00:06:34.400
extended for another week.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.734
Congratulations to you, bud!
-It's that good.

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:39.200
Really good.
-Taraji P. Henson!

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.400
"Jaja's African Hair Braiding"
is now playing

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.801
at the Samuel J. Friedman
Theater on Broadway!

